<title>UK: NFC sells cold store business to TDG.</title>
<headline>NFC sells cold store business to TDG.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>British freight transport firm NFC Plc said on Monday it had sold its remaining public cold store activities to TDG Ltd, a subsidiary of Transport Development Group Plc for 11 million stg in cash.</p>
<p>This follows the sale of NFC's Leeds cold store to Nordale Foods Ltd in May.</p>
<p>The sale is part of NFC's strategy of focusing on international logistics and moving services.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
